#! ia 1.0

@principle canon-storage-one-authority
  meaning
    says "Every mutable field has one authority, and every other copy is a derived view, an export or a link."
    answers "How many authorities may a mutable field have?"
  governance
    severity advisory
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  relationships
    cites @agent public-workspace-system-steward

@principle canon-storage-authority-before-medium
  meaning
    says "Authority is decided before medium. A store is first classified as authoritative or derived, and a derived store is rebuildable from its authority, whatever its medium or write pattern."
    answers "Is a store's authority decided before or after its medium?"
  governance
    severity advisory
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  relationships
    cites @agent public-workspace-system-steward

@convention canon-storage-review-default
  meaning
    says "When nothing is declared, authority follows review need. Content that must be reviewed and pinned before it counts has its authority where review happens: records and documents, or a database that keeps immutable reviewed revisions. Content that counts as soon as it is written, such as runtime state, events and machine output nobody reviews, has its authority where it is written."
    answers "Where is a field's authority when nothing declares it?"
  governance
    severity advisory
    requires "Absent a declaration, place the authority of reviewed-before-it-counts content where review happens, and of counts-when-written content where it is written."
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  relationships
    cites @agent public-workspace-system-steward

@convention canon-storage-declare-exceptions
  meaning
    says "Only exceptions to the review-need default are declared, through existing records. No storage-binding word exists."
    answers "Which storage authorities are declared, and through what?"
  governance
    severity advisory
    requires "Declare a store's authority only where it departs from the review-need default, and declare it through an existing record."
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  relationships
    cites @agent public-workspace-system-steward

@convention canon-storage-medium
  meaning
    says "The medium is chosen by read and write pattern: records and documents for small reviewed sets, a database for volume or concurrency. The medium never changes the authority."
    answers "How is the medium for stored content chosen?"
  governance
    severity advisory
    requires "Choose records and documents for small reviewed sets and a database for volume or concurrency, without letting the medium change the authority."
  subject
    subject-word workspace
  relationships
    cites @agent public-workspace-system-steward
